Z||000000||Philphine||02-06-2001||01:30 AM||||<BR>still waiting on bubbajoes package (pipedream?). during this time, i've been wonderng. if his mounting idea works for a 4.9, shouldn't it work for a northstar? i know there were a couple of years that they are in the same car so it seems like cadillac would have gave them similar mounting points. should whatever flywheel plan he has tranfer over too?||||reg||1
Z||000001||bHooper||02-06-2001||07:07 AM||||well, i'm certainly no engine expert... but Ed Parks is colaborating with several others, on insttalling a 4.9 liter in a fiero!<P>he has said that it is only 3/4" bigger than the 2.8 and the weight is virtually the same.  stock output being around 215 hp and 275 lbs of torque. (i believe that's what he said).<P>dont know much more than that.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||02-06-2001||08:24 AM||||FINALLY! It's been weeks since the Caddy 4.9 topic has shown up here! I think that it's one of the most overlooked conversions available to the Fiero enthousiast. I have been following Bubbajoesxx 4.9 "how to" web site as he continues its development. Although not very experienced in HTML (me neither), he seems to know his stuff about the 4.9 conversion.<P>Your question kind of perplexes me. You mention the Northstar conversion and wonder if his kit is applicable. Mounting a Northstar in a Fiero cradle is the easy part. Making it run correctly is the real challenge. <P>Your question about the flywheel is a good example. This question and hundreds more will have to answered before the car would run. What Bubba has done on his web site is give a good head start on answering those types of questions for the 4.9. <P>I'd say if you really had your heart set on a Northstar, look to those sites that feature this conversion. If you do a search on Northstar, you may be able to find a couple of links to sites (like Bubba's) where the conversion is explained. Or, maybe, someone has them marked on their Favorites and can pass them along.<P>Good luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||10
Z||000003||bHooper||02-06-2001||08:50 AM||||whats this fellas web site?  anyone got the address?<P>thanks!<BR>hoop||||reg||7
Z||000004||CozmoPooky||02-06-2001||09:27 AM||||Here's his site... <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/</A> <BR>He's currently doing another conversion as well as updating his website almost daily.  I'm going to start the swap on the Duke Coupe in the next month or so using his procedure.  Bubbajoexxx has got a good grip on the process and is a great example of the true spirit of streetrodding.  I agree with Roy, the Caddy engine is a fine match for the Fiero.  The next phase is to get more horsepower from it when it's finally installed (so what else is new?) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>CozmoPooky<BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>'87 Duke Coupe     <BR>'85 2M6 Targa<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/bothfierossig1.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000005||MooCow||02-06-2001||11:03 AM||||Ed Parks was going to make this into a kit you could buy yourself but he said that there is to much welding that has to be done.  He doesn't even have the a 4.9 in a car yet and he hopes to have one done by teh swap meet.  He has three going at once.  One in an 88 craddle with a 5 speed. Another in an 88 with a Fiero automatic, and the final one I think is on an 88 or 87 amd uses the 4.9 caddy tranny.  He will let me know more info as he goes along.  After he does this one he is doing another one to see if he is able to make a kit out of it.  I will let you know more when I know more.<BR>Also he drove one already and said that is about 1 second faster than my car useing the 4.9 auto tranny.  My car is a 3.4 with a 4:10 gear ratio and hauls a$$ but I don't have no times yet.<P>                              Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
