Z||000009||lou_dias||02-07-2001||08:11 AM||||CozmoPooky,<BR>  The trick is to get more power out of it before you put it in not after.  I think someone should start looking up a perfomance rebuild for that motor.  With that much torque, I would go for a high HP rebuild.  Port the heads and intake and get a high revving cam.  If you could get 255hp and 275 ft*lbs out of it, that would be sweet.  And it should be attainable too.  It would smoke the 3800SC's...||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phil||02-07-2001||09:30 AM||||A series II SC3800 with a pulley change will put out about 275 hp and running a 5 sp puts 222hp and 273ft-lbs to the wheels(dyno tested)||||reg||1
Z||000011||CozmoPooky||02-07-2001||10:23 AM||||I wonder if you did the "usual suspects", (i.e. head work, match intake/exhaust, etc.) what the gains would be...<BR>Haven't found very much performance info on this engine, been checking the Caddy <A HREF="http://www.mts.simplenet.com/Ring/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mts.simplenet.com/Ring/</A> <BR>and J-body forums <A HREF="http://www.j-body.org/index.php" TARGET=_blank>http://www.j-body.org/index.php</A> <BR>with little success. I'm looking into this, any help or ideas would be great!<BR>CozmoPooky||||reg||1
Z||000012||Philphine||02-07-2001||11:36 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/stars/mycaddy/asg.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/stars/mycaddy/asg.htm</A> <P><BR>i'm batting 1000 for not putting addys in right. maybe i got it this time. this place came out the last round of 4.9 threads. actually i thought it was cosmo who found it, but maybe it was some one else. they're getting something close to 290hp out of 4.9's.||||reg||1
Z||000013||rockcrawl||02-07-2001||05:32 PM||||I bought a complete 91 Cadillac DeVille, 4.9, light front hit, 130k miles, runs and drives great. I paid $350 for the entire car. You won't touch a SC 3800 for that price. And remember you'll need to replace that supercharger at 80k miles when it wears out, or make that 50k with the pulley change. I'm not knocking the 3.8, it's a terrific engine, but it's not a cheap engine, and it's no V8. My dad had a 4.1 Caddy with over 250k miles on it and running strong, I still have that engine. My first consideration for any engine swap is power increase per dollar. Compare the 4.9 with the N* and 3800, and you'll see the 4.9 can't be beat hp/dollar. I would imagine it is also the lightest. BTW the Cad 4.1, 4.5, 4.9 use the same firing order as a small block, so they have the same rumble when you remove the restrictive Caddy exhaust.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
